# Run every day at 5 AM Eastern Standard Time.
#
# The timeout matters as much as the schedule. supercronic will not start a
# second instance of a job while the first is still running, so a run that
# hangs silently suppresses every run after it. That happened: a run begun on
# 19 August was still alive thirteen days later, and no data was ingested in
# between.
0 10 * * * timeout 3600 /usr/local/bin/fbo_scraper
